<title>CROATIA: Croatia Jan RPI rises to 1.0 pct, 4.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Croatia Jan RPI rises to 1.0 pct, 4.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State Bureau of Statistics issued the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> CROATIA RETAIL PRICES	 JANUARY     DEC '96	JAN '96</p>
<p> Monthly change (pct)	   +1.0	   0.0	   +0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +4.2	  +3.5	   +3.2</p>
<p>NOTES -- January retail prices were 2.6 percent higher than the 1996 average. Retail price inflation was 3.5 percent last year compared to 1995.</p>
<p>Croatia introduced a radical anti-inflation programme in October 1993, when monthly inflation hit 38.7 percent.</p>
<p>-- Kolumbina Bencevic, Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
